 "narrative": "The second discovery batch screened six predictors on outcome_011 and outcome_014. Using signed evidence, positive estimates indicate that the exposed group has more negative dependency scores, i.e., stronger CRISPR dependency, which is the hypothesized meaningful direction. The approximate 10% absolute-mean thresholds were 0.0301 for outcome_011 and 0.0093 for outcome_014. Most screened comparisons were small, had intervals crossing zero, and did not support a clinically meaningful negative dependency-score shift. These include feature_054, feature_045, feature_008, feature_047, and feature_021; I reject those exact main-effect claims and close them, while acknowledging that subgroup or outcome-specific effects are not ruled out. Feature_032=1 versus 0 is the only promising predictor. On outcome_011 (H35/R23), the signed point estimate is +0.0351, slightly above threshold, but the interval [-0.0225, +0.0928] crosses zero and is wide; this is unresolved but deferred. On outcome_014 (H36/R24), the signed point estimate is +0.0685, far above the small outcome_014 threshold of 0.0093, and the interval [-0.0012, +0.1381] barely includes zero. This is clinically promising but imprecise, based on only 110 exposed observations, and one of 12 new screens, so I do not accept it on discovery evidence alone. I request independent validation for H36 to determine whether the feature_032 association with stronger outcome_014 dependency is robust.",
 "research_notes": "Current status: no accepted claims. H1-H12 remain rejected/closed. H15,H16,H19,H20,H23,H24,H27,H28,H31,H32 rejected/closed as unsupported feature_054/045/008/047/021 main effects on outcome_011 or outcome_014. H35 (feature_032 on outcome_011) is unresolved/deferred: point estimate +0.0351, interval crosses zero, threshold ~0.0301. H36 (feature_032 on outcome_014) is unresolved/active and requested for validation: point estimate +0.0685, interval [-0.0012,0.1381], threshold ~0.0093, exposed n=110. If validation supports H36, prioritize feature_032 expansion across other outcomes, especially already registered outcome_001/outcome_006 claims, and assess consistency rather than treating outcome_014 alone as established. If validation fails, close feature_032 as unsupported or fragile and return to broader binary/categorical predictor screening. Avoid validation for small or imprecise main effects."
}

