  "narrative": "This batch tests six binary predictors on outcome_002 and outcome_015. With direction -1, signed positive estimates mean stronger CRISPR dependency in the exposed group. Approximate absolute-mean 10% clinical thresholds are 0.0260 for outcome_002 and 0.0250 for outcome_015. Most results are near null, cross zero, or have point estimates far below the clinical threshold, and the entire positive interval often remains below the 10% magnitude. I therefore reject and close H67-H69 and H71-H75 and H77-H78 as exact comparisons in this dataset. These rejections do not exclude subgroup, interaction, thresholded, or other outcome-specific effects.\n\nTwo comparisons are borderline candidates. H70, feature_034=1 versus 0 on outcome_015, has signed estimate +0.0170, interval [0.0017, 0.0323], corresponding to about 6.8% of the absolute outcome mean. It is the only comparison in this batch with a 95% discovery interval excluding zero, but the point estimate is still below the 10% clinical threshold, although the interval includes clinically meaningful positive values. Because it is a well-powered contrast with good cell sizes and the most defensible signal among the twelve tests, I keep it unresolved and request independent validation. The prior false-positive/validation failure in this run makes validation appropriate here, especially given the multiplicity of the twelve-test screen. I do not accept it yet because the discovery point estimate does not meet the clinically meaningful magnitude and one nominal result among many could be noise.\n\nH76, feature_027=1 versus 0 on outcome_015, has signed estimate +0.0177, interval [-0.0016, 0.0369], also about 7.1% of the absolute outcome mean. It is suggestive but weaker because the interval crosses zero by a small amount and its point estimate is below threshold. I defer it rather than validating it, because H70 is the stronger candidate and validation capacity should be reserved. The remaining comparisons are either opposite direction, null, or imprecise and not clinically meaningful. These are observational associations within the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
