  "narrative": "H303 is reassessed now that independent validation R268 is available. For the registered direction, both discovery and validation are positive in signed units, but the validation does not provide robust practical evidence. Discovery R256 was signed +0.0357 with 95% interval +0.0070 to +0.0644, so it supported the direction but its lower bound was far below the roughly 0.025 absolute dependency-score threshold implied by a 10% relative difference for outcome_012. Independent validation R268 is signed +0.0337, with independent interval -0.0128 to +0.0802. That interval includes zero, includes clinically negligible and opposite-direction effects, and therefore does not confirm a scientifically meaningful association at the stringent validation scale. Given the large correlated-outcome multiplicity, the pre-specified practical threshold, and the inconsistent feature_028 family (H304 was interval-exclusive but opposite to the registered hypothesis; H305-H308 were null or near-null), I reject H303 as unsupported and close feature_028 as a clinically meaningful dependency-score association.\n\nFinal scientific report for the accumulated evidence. The accepted claim set remains empty. The strongest supportable conclusion from this supplied dataset is a bounded negative one: across the tested binary, high-prevalence categorical, rare-level categorical, subgroup-interaction, and eligibility-stratified comparisons of 16 CRISPR dependency-score outcomes, no predictor or subgroup showed a robust association with a scientifically meaningful dependency-score difference under the stated 10% relative-difference practical benchmark. The tested predictor families include common binary markers such as feature_002, feature_034, feature_060, feature_042, feature_045, feature_008, feature_047, feature_021, feature_032, feature_063, feature_048 level_001 versus level_003, feature_054 level_002 versus level_001, feature_055 level contrasts, and now feature_028 level_001 versus level_003 plus feature_036 level_001 versus level_002. Most estimates were near zero, interval-inclusive, opposite to the registered hypothesis, or compatible with clinically negligible effects. Tested interactions and conditioned contrasts involving feature_010, feature_015, feature_040, feature_051, feature_034, feature_002, and feature_060 also did not produce robust clinically meaningful subgroup differences.\n\nIndependent validation did not rescue the borderline candidate signals. Prior validations of candidates including H1, H36, H70, H77, H85, H240, H246, H247, H251, H252, H253, and now H303 failed to provide robust evidence for a practical association: intervals either included zero, included negligible or opposite effects, or failed the practical-scale requirement. The reversed low-prevalence candidate claims were not validated, and the final feature_028 candidate H303 is now closed as unsupported.\n\nNegative findings include: (1) null main effects for the tested common binary predictors on screened dependency outcomes; (2) null high-prevalence categorical level contrasts for feature_054, feature_055, feature_063, feature_048 level_001 versus level_003, feature_028, and feature_036; (3) no robust registered stronger-dependency signal in the feature_042 panel; and (4) failed validation of earlier low-prevalence or borderline candidates, including feature_007, feature_029, feature_032/outcome_014, and feature_028/outcome_012. Several nominal or interval-borderline discoveries remain in the ledger, but they are not accepted because their intervals remain compatible with subthreshold effects, their direction is opposite to the registered claim, they arose in a high-multiplicity correlated-outcome setting, or independent validation did not support them.\n\nInterpretation remains dataset-specific and observational. These results do not prove that the predictors cannot influence CRISPR dependency, nor do they identify biological mechanism, clinical causality, or external generalizability. The predictors are opaque, the outcomes are correlated, many tests were performed, and all contrasts are marginal unadjusted comparisons. Power is limited for outcome_006 and outcome_014 because of larger dispersion and shifted means, and rare categorical levels remain difficult to evaluate under the 20-per-cell rule.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is to use any remaining analysis budget to complete the already registered feature_045 main-effect panel H315-H320 across outcome_012, outcome_005, outcome_015, outcome_002, outcome_016, and outcome_007, applying the same strict acceptance rule: support requires an interval that both supports the registered direction and excludes clinically negligible values. If that panel is null, close the broad univariate binary/categorical discovery screen as negative for the tested predictors. Further work should then shift away from marginal univariate mining toward pre-specified continuous-predictor dose-response or threshold analyses, adjusted multivariate models, targeted external validation of any strong pre-specified hypotheses, or independent cohorts with higher power.",
  "research_notes": "H303 rejected and closed after independent validation failed: validation R268 signed estimate +0.0337 with interval -0.0128 to +0.0802; includes zero and subthreshold effects. Discovery R256 was +0.0357 with interval +0.0070 to +0.0644, but lower bound below practical threshold and inconsistent with other feature_028 outcomes. Feature_028 screen closed negative.\n\nCurrent accepted claim set remains empty. The broad univariate binary/categorical screen is now essentially complete for feature_002, feature_034, feature_060, feature_042, feature_008, feature_047, feature_021, feature_032, feature_063, feature_048, feature_054, feature_055, feature_028, and feature_036, with feature_045 still pending via active H315-H320. Next analysis priority: complete H315-H320 feature_045 panel if controller selects it; require interval-exclusive practical evidence before acceptance. If null, close feature_045 and the univariate discovery screen. No further validation requests for feature_028. Future follow-up should focus on continuous predictors, adjusted models, or external validation rather than more marginal categorical mining."
}

